  "interpretation": "For each empty cell, all old collinear-pair blockers are disjoint because the validated seed has no collinear triple. At least one deletion per blocker is necessary, and selecting one old point from each disjoint blocker is sufficient for inserting that cell alone. If this minimum exceeds the deletion budget, deleting at most that many seed points cannot admit any genuinely new point. This prunes only those seed-relative repair budgets; it is neither a global bound nor an impossibility result for larger deletions, other seeds, or other constructions.",
